   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c00",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "# BigCommerce Merchant Payment Intelligence Scorer\n\n> **A lightweight scoring model that prioritises payment methods for BigCommerce merchants based on segment, geography, AOV, and mobile footprint.**\n\n**Author:** Ben Drayton | **Built:** June 2026\n**Context:** Portfolio artefact demonstrating applied payments product thinking for Commerce (BigCommerce) Senior PM, Payments role.\n\n---\n\n## The Problem\n\nMost BigCommerce merchants choose payment methods reactively — enable Stripe, add PayPal, maybe Afterpay because a friend recommended it. The selection is rarely driven by structured analysis of who their customers are, what they're buying, where they are, or how they pay.\n\nThe consequence is predictable: checkout conversion left on the table, processing costs higher than necessary, and payment method mix that doesn't map to the merchant's actual growth levers.\n\nThis notebook changes that. Given a merchant profile, it evaluates **14 payment methods** available on BigCommerce across **8 dimensions weighted to match the merchant's context**. Output: a prioritised action list with rationale.\n\n---\n\n## Data Sources\n\nBuilt against BigCommerce's live ecosystem as of June 2026:\n\n- [BC developer docs — Payments API](https://developer.bigcommerce.com/docs/store-operations/payments)\n- [BC payment gateways — US](https://www.bigcommerce.com/payments/gateways/united-states)\n- [BC payment gateways — Australia](https://www.bigcommerce.com/payments/gateways/australia)\n- [Commerce Live EMEA 2026 product roadmap](https://www.bigcommerce.com/blog/commerce-live-emea-2026/) — agentic commerce, Stripe partnership, Adyen sponsorship\n- [BigCommerce × Stripe Agentic Commerce Suite](https://investors.bigcommerce.com/news-releases/news-release-details/bigcommerce-partners-stripe-support-new-agentic-commerce-suite)\n- [github.com/bigcommerce/checkout-sdk-js](https://github.com/bigcommerce/checkout-sdk-js) — Checkout SDK for custom and agent-driven flows"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c01",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## Scoring Dimensions\n\nEach payment method is scored **1–5** per dimension. Scores are then weighted according to the merchant's priorities.\n\n| Dimension | What it measures |\n|---|---|\n| `bc_native` | How natively integrated is this in the BC control panel? (5 = one-click, no dev) |\n| `b2c_fit` | Does this method match B2C consumer checkout expectations? |\n| `b2b_fit` | Does it support enterprise purchasing patterns — invoicing, ACH, net terms? |\n| `aov_fit` | Does the merchant's AOV fall in this method's documented sweet spot? |\n| `geo_coverage` | What fraction of the merchant's active markets does this method support? |\n| `mobile_agentic` | Is it SDK-compatible? Does it work in agent-driven checkout flows? |\n| `conversion_uplift` | Evidence-based estimated conversion lift, normalised 0–5 |\n| `impl_complexity` | How fast can a BC merchant activate this? (5 = trivial, 1 = heavy custom build) |\n\n> **Zero-weighted dimensions** are intentionally excluded per profile — they signal what *not* to optimise for in that merchant's context."
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "c02",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": "import pandas as pd\nimport textwrap\n\npd.set_option(\"display.max_colwidth\", 90)\npd.set_option(\"display.width\", 180)"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "c03",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": "# ─── Payment Methods Database ──────────────────────────────────────────────────\n#\n# 14 methods sourced from BigCommerce's live gateway pages and developer docs (June 2026).\n# US gateway list: Adyen, Affirm, Afterpay, Amazon Pay, Authorize.net, Bolt,\n#   Chase, Checkout.com, Clover, CyberSource, Heartland, Klarna, PayPal, Braintree,\n#   SecureNet, Sezzle, Square, Stripe, WorldPay, Zip (Quadpay), + 15 others\n# AU gateway list: Adyen, Afterpay, Checkout.com, CommBank (MIGS), eWAY, Humm,\n#   Klarna, Laybuy, OpenPay, PayPal, Braintree, Sezzle, Square, Stripe, Windcave, Zip\n#\n# bc_native scores:\n#   5 = native control panel (one-click, no dev)\n#   4 = native partner (pre-integrated, minimal config)\n#   3 = partner integration (supported gateway)\n#   2 = B2B Edition feature\n#   1 = custom / headless only\n\nPAYMENT_METHODS = {\n    \"BC Payments (PayPal)\": {\n        \"bc_native\": 5, \"bc_integration_type\": \"Native — control panel\",\n        \"b2c_fit\": 4, \"b2b_fit\": 2,\n        \"aov_sweet_spot\": (10, 500),\n        \"geo_coverage\": [\"US\"],\n        \"mobile_agentic\": 4, \"conversion_lift_pct\": 8, \"impl_complexity\": 5,\n        \"note\": (\n            \"Embedded solution powered by PayPal. Single on-site flow includes \"\n            \"Apple Pay, Google Pay, Afterpay, Klarna, Venmo, PayPal Pay Later. \"\n            \"US-only (Standard/Plus/Pro). Announced at Commerce Live 2026.\"\n        ),\n    },\n    \"Stripe\": {\n        \"bc_native\": 4, \"bc_integration_type\": \"Native partner\",\n        \"b2c_fit\": 5, \"b2b_fit\": 4,\n        \"aov_sweet_spot\": (10, 50000),\n        \"geo_coverage\": [\"US\", \"AU\", \"UK\", \"EU\", \"GLOBAL\"],\n        \"mobile_agentic\": 5, \"conversion_lift_pct\": 6, \"impl_complexity\": 4,\n        \"note\": (\n            \"BC's designated partner for the Agentic Commerce Suite (Commerce Live 2026). \"\n            \"Stripe Link for accelerated guest checkout. \"\n            \"Supports OCS, ACH, stored instruments, and agentic cart/checkout via the \"\n            \"checkout-sdk-js (github.com/bigcommerce/checkout-sdk-js). \"\n            \"Payments API rate limit: 50 req / 4 sec.\"\n        ),\n    },\n    \"Adyen\": {\n        \"bc_native\": 3, \"bc_integration_type\": \"Native partner\",\n        \"b2c_fit\": 4, \"b2b_fit\": 4,\n        \"aov_sweet_spot\": (100, 100000),\n        \"geo_coverage\": [\"US\", \"AU\", \"UK\", \"EU\", \"GLOBAL\"],\n        \"mobile_agentic\": 4, \"conversion_lift_pct\": 5, \"impl_complexity\": 3,\n        \"note\": (\n            \"Title sponsor of Commerce Live EMEA 2026. Adyen UK MD presented on \"\n            \"agentic commerce infrastructure from a payments provider perspective. \"\n            \"Named as BC's Growth Champion Partner award winner. \"\n            \"Strong local payment method coverage; preferred for multi-geo enterprise.\"\n        ),\n    },\n    \"PayPal Commerce Platform\": {\n        \"bc_native\": 4, \"bc_integration_type\": \"Native partner\",\n        \"b2c_fit\": 5, \"b2b_fit\": 2,\n        \"aov_sweet_spot\": (10, 500),\n        \"geo_coverage\": [\"US\", \"AU\", \"UK\", \"EU\", \"GLOBAL\"],\n        \"mobile_agentic\": 3, \"conversion_lift_pct\": 7, \"impl_complexity\": 4,\n        \"note\": (\n            \"Standalone from BC Payments bundle. High consumer trust globally. \"\n            \"Fastlane by PayPal available for accelerated guest checkout. \"\n            \"Also underpins BC Payments (US) as primary processor.\"\n        ),\n    },\n    \"Afterpay / Clearpay\": {\n        \"bc_native\": 3, \"bc_integration_type\": \"Native partner\",\n        \"b2c_fit\": 5, \"b2b_fit\": 1,\n        \"aov_sweet_spot\": (30, 500),\n        \"geo_coverage\": [\"US\", \"AU\", \"UK\"],\n        \"mobile_agentic\": 3, \"conversion_lift_pct\": 15, \"impl_complexity\": 4,\n        \"note\": (\n            \"AU-originator BNPL. ~15% documented conversion + AOV uplift in $30–$500 range. \"\n            \"Available standalone or bundled inside BC Payments (US). \"\n            \"Listed natively on BC's AU gateway page.\"\n        ),\n    },\n    \"Klarna\": {\n        \"bc_native\": 3, \"bc_integration_type\": \"Native partner\",\n        \"b2c_fit\": 5, \"b2b_fit\": 2,\n        \"aov_sweet_spot\": (30, 1500),\n        \"geo_coverage\": [\"US\", \"AU\", \"UK\", \"EU\"],\n        \"mobile_agentic\": 3, \"conversion_lift_pct\": 12, \"impl_complexity\": 4,\n        \"note\": (\n            \"Broader BNPL AOV range than Afterpay — stronger above $500. \"\n            \"Dominant in EU/UK. Included in BC Payments bundle (US). \"\n            \"Listed on AU gateway page.\"\n        ),\n    },\n    \"Affirm\": {\n        \"bc_native\": 3, \"bc_integration_type\": \"Native partner\",\n        \"b2c_fit\": 4, \"b2b_fit\": 1,\n        \"aov_sweet_spot\": (100, 3000),\n        \"geo_coverage\": [\"US\"],\n        \"mobile_agentic\": 3, \"conversion_lift_pct\": 10, \"impl_complexity\": 4,\n        \"note\": (\n            \"US-only. Better segment fit than Afterpay/Klarna for $100–$3k AOV range. \"\n            \"Listed on BC US gateway page natively.\"\n        ),\n    },\n    \"Amazon Pay\": {\n        \"bc_native\": 4, \"bc_integration_type\": \"Native partner\",\n        \"b2c_fit\": 4, \"b2b_fit\": 2,\n        \"aov_sweet_spot\": (20, 500),\n        \"geo_coverage\": [\"US\", \"UK\", \"EU\"],\n        \"mobile_agentic\": 3, \"conversion_lift_pct\": 5, \"impl_complexity\": 4,\n        \"note\": (\n            \"Leverages Amazon account trust and stored payment/address data. \"\n            \"Strong for Prime-aligned consumer segments. \"\n            \"Mentioned in BC's digital wallets accelerated checkout capability.\"\n        ),\n    },\n    \"Apple Pay / Google Pay\": {\n        \"bc_native\": 4, \"bc_integration_type\": \"Native via gateway\",\n        \"b2c_fit\": 5, \"b2b_fit\": 2,\n        \"aov_sweet_spot\": (10, 300),\n        \"geo_coverage\": [\"US\", \"AU\", \"UK\", \"EU\", \"GLOBAL\"],\n        \"mobile_agentic\": 5, \"conversion_lift_pct\": 10, \"impl_complexity\": 4,\n        \"note\": (\n            \"Enabled via Stripe, BC Payments (US), or Braintree — no separate gateway. \"\n            \"Critical for mobile conversion and agentic checkout interfaces — \"\n            \"Commerce's explicitly stated 2026 strategic direction. \"\n            \"Eliminates form-fill friction on mobile; required for agentic one-tap flows.\"\n        ),\n    },\n    \"ACH / Bank Transfer\": {\n        \"bc_native\": 3, \"bc_integration_type\": \"Native via gateway\",\n        \"b2c_fit\": 2, \"b2b_fit\": 5,\n        \"aov_sweet_spot\": (500, 500000),\n        \"geo_coverage\": [\"US\"],\n        \"mobile_agentic\": 3, \"conversion_lift_pct\": 8, \"impl_complexity\": 3,\n        \"note\": (\n            \"US ACH via Stripe (bank debit) or Braintree. \"\n            \"Dominant B2B payment rail for high-AOV transactions. \"\n            \"Eliminates ~2.9% card processing fee — material at enterprise order values. \"\n            \"BC Payments API supports stored instruments for recurring ACH.\"\n        ),\n    },\n    \"B2B Invoice / Net Terms\": {\n        \"bc_native\": 2, \"bc_integration_type\": \"B2B Edition\",\n        \"b2c_fit\": 1, \"b2b_fit\": 5,\n        \"aov_sweet_spot\": (1000, 1000000),\n        \"geo_coverage\": [\"US\", \"AU\", \"UK\", \"EU\", \"GLOBAL\"],\n        \"mobile_agentic\": 2, \"conversion_lift_pct\": 20, \"impl_complexity\": 2,\n        \"note\": (\n            \"BC B2B Edition supports net terms and invoice payment natively. \"\n            \"'B2B automation and pricing' was a headline item in Commerce Live 2026 roadmap. \"\n            \"Removes payment as a blocker in enterprise sales cycles — \"\n            \"highest potential lift for B2B merchants on this list.\"\n        ),\n    },\n    \"Zip / Quadpay\": {\n        \"bc_native\": 3, \"bc_integration_type\": \"Native partner\",\n        \"b2c_fit\": 4, \"b2b_fit\": 1,\n        \"aov_sweet_spot\": (30, 1000),\n        \"geo_coverage\": [\"US\", \"AU\"],\n        \"mobile_agentic\": 3, \"conversion_lift_pct\": 8, \"impl_complexity\": 4,\n        \"note\": (\n            \"AU-originator; listed natively on BC AU gateway page. \"\n            \"Growing US presence under Zip brand (formerly Quadpay). \"\n            \"Good complement to Afterpay for AU merchants.\"\n        ),\n    },\n    \"Checkout.com\": {\n        \"bc_native\": 3, \"bc_integration_type\": \"Native partner\",\n        \"b2c_fit\": 4, \"b2b_fit\": 3,\n        \"aov_sweet_spot\": (20, 100000),\n        \"geo_coverage\": [\"US\", \"AU\", \"UK\", \"EU\", \"GLOBAL\"],\n        \"mobile_agentic\": 3, \"conversion_lift_pct\": 4, \"impl_complexity\": 3,\n        \"note\": (\n            \"Listed on BC AU and US gateway pages. \"\n            \"Strong for high-volume international enterprise; \"\n            \"competitive fraud tooling and local payment method depth.\"\n        ),\n    },\n    \"Square\": {\n        \"bc_native\": 4, \"bc_integration_type\": \"Native partner\",\n        \"b2c_fit\": 4, \"b2b_fit\": 2,\n        \"aov_sweet_spot\": (10, 500),\n        \"geo_coverage\": [\"US\", \"AU\", \"UK\"],\n        \"mobile_agentic\": 3, \"conversion_lift_pct\": 3, \"impl_complexity\": 5,\n        \"note\": (\n            \"Best for omnichannel merchants running POS + online from one account. \"\n            \"Lowest setup friction of any gateway on this list. \"\n            \"Listed on AU and US BC gateway pages natively.\"\n        ),\n    },\n}"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "c04",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": "# ─── Merchant Profiles ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n#\n# Weights reflect priorities for each merchant's context and sum to 1.0.\n# Zero-weighted dimensions are intentionally excluded — signal of what NOT\n# to optimise for in that context.\n\nMERCHANT_PROFILES = {\n    \"smb_apparel_b2c\": {\n        \"name\": \"SMB Apparel — B2C (US, AOV $85)\",\n        \"description\": \"Fashion retailer, US market, 72% mobile traffic, growing DTC brand\",\n        \"segment\": \"B2C\", \"geography\": [\"US\"],\n        \"avg_order_value\": 85, \"mobile_traffic_pct\": 72, \"b2b_pct\": 0,\n        \"bc_plan\": \"Plus\",\n        \"current_methods\": [\"Stripe\", \"PayPal Commerce Platform\"],\n        \"weights\": {\n            \"conversion_uplift\": 0.30,  # Primary lever: add-to-cart → purchase\n            \"mobile_agentic\":    0.25,  # 72% mobile — wallet + agent-readiness critical\n            \"b2c_fit\":           0.15,  # Consumer checkout method alignment\n            \"aov_fit\":           0.10,  # Determines BNPL eligibility: Afterpay ($30–$500) vs Affirm ($100–$3k)\n            \"bc_native\":         0.10,\n            \"impl_complexity\":   0.10,  # SMB: time to value matters\n            \"b2b_fit\":           0.00,  # Not relevant\n            \"geo_coverage\":      0.00,  # US-only — not a differentiator\n        },\n    },\n    \"b2b_software_enterprise\": {\n        \"name\": \"B2B SaaS — Enterprise (US + AU, AOV $2,400)\",\n        \"description\": \"Enterprise software, complex sales cycle, annual contracts, 90% B2B\",\n        \"segment\": \"B2B\", \"geography\": [\"US\", \"AU\"],\n        \"avg_order_value\": 2400, \"mobile_traffic_pct\": 25, \"b2b_pct\": 90,\n        \"bc_plan\": \"Enterprise\",\n        \"current_methods\": [\"Stripe\", \"PayPal Commerce Platform\"],\n        \"weights\": {\n            \"b2b_fit\":           0.40,  # B2B payment behaviour dominates; procurement compatibility is binary\n            \"aov_fit\":           0.25,  # High-AOV enterprise: method must support $2,400+ transactions\n            \"conversion_uplift\": 0.15,  # Conversion lift is a B2C metric; B2B lift is compliance, not persuasion\n            \"geo_coverage\":      0.10,  # US + AU both active\n            \"bc_native\":         0.05,\n            \"impl_complexity\":   0.05,  # Enterprise absorbs implementation effort\n            \"mobile_agentic\":    0.00,  # Desktop-dominant\n            \"b2c_fit\":           0.00,\n        },\n    },\n    \"multi_geo_marketplace\": {\n        \"name\": \"Multi-Geo Marketplace (US / UK / AU, AOV $150)\",\n        \"description\": \"B2B+B2C marketplace expanding internationally, mixed segment\",\n        \"segment\": \"B2B+B2C\", \"geography\": [\"US\", \"UK\", \"AU\"],\n        \"avg_order_value\": 150, \"mobile_traffic_pct\": 55, \"b2b_pct\": 35,\n        \"bc_plan\": \"Enterprise\",\n        \"current_methods\": [\"Stripe\", \"PayPal Commerce Platform\", \"Afterpay / Clearpay\"],\n        \"weights\": {\n            \"geo_coverage\":      0.20,  # Multi-market reach is the binding constraint\n            \"conversion_uplift\": 0.20,\n            \"b2c_fit\":           0.20,  # 65% B2C volume justifies equal weight with geo\n            \"mobile_agentic\":    0.15,  # 55% mobile + Commerce's agentic direction\n            \"b2b_fit\":           0.10,  # 35% B2B — material but secondary\n            \"aov_fit\":           0.05,\n            \"bc_native\":         0.05,\n            \"impl_complexity\":   0.05,  # Enterprise can absorb; non-zero rewards easy wins\n        },\n    },\n}"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "c05",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": "# ─── Scoring Engine ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\ndef score_aov_fit(aov: float, aov_min: float, aov_max: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Score how well merchant AOV falls within the method's sweet spot.\"\"\"\n    if aov_min <= aov <= aov_max:\n        return 5.0\n    elif aov < aov_min:\n        gap = (aov_min - aov) / aov_min\n        return max(1.0, round(5 * (1 - gap), 1))\n    else:\n        gap = (aov - aov_max) / aov_max\n        return max(1.0, round(5 * (1 - min(gap, 0.8)), 1))\n\n\ndef score_geo(merchant_geos: list, method_geos: list) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Fraction of merchant's active markets covered by this method.\"\"\"\n    if \"GLOBAL\" in method_geos:\n        return 5.0\n    covered = sum(1 for g in merchant_geos if g in method_geos)\n    return round((covered / len(merchant_geos)) * 5, 1)\n\n\ndef lift_to_score(lift_pct: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Normalise conversion lift % → 0–5 score (20%+ = 5).\"\"\"\n    return min(5.0, round(lift_pct / 4.0, 1))\n\n\ndef score_method(key: str, method: dict, merchant: dict) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Score one payment method against a merchant profile.\"\"\"\n    w = merchant[\"weights\"]\n    aov = merchant[\"avg_order_value\"]\n\n    s = {\n        \"bc_native\":         float(method[\"bc_native\"]),\n        \"b2c_fit\":           float(method[\"b2c_fit\"]),\n        \"b2b_fit\":           float(method[\"b2b_fit\"]),\n        \"aov_fit\":           score_aov_fit(aov, *method[\"aov_sweet_spot\"]),\n        \"geo_coverage\":      score_geo(merchant[\"geography\"], method[\"geo_coverage\"]),\n        \"mobile_agentic\":    float(method[\"mobile_agentic\"]),\n        \"conversion_uplift\": lift_to_score(method[\"conversion_lift_pct\"]),\n        \"impl_complexity\":   float(method[\"impl_complexity\"]),\n    }\n\n    total = sum(s[d] * w[d] for d in w)\n\n    if s[\"geo_coverage\"] == 0:\n        total = 0.0\n        rec = \"❌  Not available in merchant's markets\"\n    elif key in merchant.get(\"current_methods\", []):\n        rec = \"✅  Already active\"\n    elif total >= 3.5:\n        rec = \"🚀  High priority — add this\"\n    elif total >= 2.0:\n        rec = \"💡  Worth evaluating\"\n    else:\n        rec = \"⬇   Low priority\"\n\n    return {\n        \"Payment Method\": key,\n        \"Score /5\":       round(total, 2),\n        \"Action\":         rec,\n        \"BC Integration\": method[\"bc_integration_type\"],\n        \"Est. Lift\":      f\"+{method['conversion_lift_pct']}%\",\n        \"Notes\":          method[\"note\"],\n    }\n\n\ndef run_analysis(profile_key: str) -> pd.DataFrame:\n    \"\"\"Score all 14 payment methods for a merchant profile. Print results.\"\"\"\n    m = MERCHANT_PROFILES[profile_key]\n\n    print()\n    print(\"=\" * 82)\n    print(f\"  {m['name']}\")\n    print(f\"  {m['description']}\")\n    print(\"=\" * 82)\n    print(f\"  Segment: {m['segment']}  |  Markets: {', '.join(m['geography'])}  |  \"\n          f\"AOV: ${m['avg_order_value']:,}  |  Mobile: {m['mobile_traffic_pct']}%  |  \"\n          f\"BC Plan: {m['bc_plan']}\")\n    print()\n\n    results = [score_method(k, v, m) for k, v in PAYMENT_METHODS.items()]\n    df = pd.DataFrame(results).sort_values(\"Score /5\", ascending=False).reset_index(drop=True)\n    df.index += 1\n\n    cols = [\"Payment Method\", \"Score /5\", \"Action\", \"BC Integration\", \"Est. Lift\"]\n    print(df[cols].to_string())\n    print()\n\n    high = df[df[\"Action\"].str.contains(\"High priority\", na=False)]\n    if not high.empty:\n        print(\"── High Priority — Rationale \" + \"─\" * 52)\n        for _, row in high.iterrows():\n            print(f\"\\n  {row['Payment Method']}  (Score: {row['Score /5']})\")\n            for line in textwrap.wrap(row[\"Notes\"], 74):\n                print(f\"    {line}\")\n        print()\n\n    return df"
  },
  {
